+/* SPU PUTs into RSX local memory (0xC0000000, 256 MB) since the walker last
+ * looked: the 1 MB pieces they touched. The heap poll a passed semaphore runs
+ * covers main memory only, so a table an SPU job writes into VRAM just before
+ * its release (Into the Nexus: per-object 8x8 FP16 lighting, job 42A41602)
+ * stayed "unwritten" until the next full poll and draws in between used the
+ * cached copy ([verify] "changed with no write seen" on 0x024Exxxx 8x8 fmt
+ * 0xBA; owner's Thram "black flashes", 2026-11-16). Noted from the SPU
+ * threads (a plain byte store; a missed note falls back to the next full
+ * poll, as before), polled on the walker after the heap poll, same epoch. */
